/-
  IP.Crypto.AES — pure-data AES-128 (FIPS 197).

  State: 16 bytes treated as a 4×4 matrix, column-major.
  Operations: SubBytes (S-box), ShiftRows, MixColumns,
  AddRoundKey, KeyExpansion (Rcon, RotWord, SubWord).

  AES-128: 10 rounds, 11 round keys (each 16 bytes).
  Round structure:
    AddRoundKey(state, K_0)
    for r in 1..9:
      SubBytes; ShiftRows; MixColumns; AddRoundKey(K_r)
    SubBytes; ShiftRows; AddRoundKey(K_10)

  Decrypt is the inverse: InvShiftRows, InvSubBytes,
  AddRoundKey, InvMixColumns (with the round-key schedule
  iterated in reverse).

  Validated against FIPS 197 Appendix B (128-bit KAT).
-/

import Sparkle

namespace Sparkle.IP.Crypto.AES

/-! ### S-box and inverse S-box (FIPS 197 §5.1.1 / Figure 7). -/

